  "items": [
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3my4xspgnf22t",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "In a move that is both fascinating and viscerally unsettling, AI world model company Odyssey took a simulation of a fruit fly's brain, Google's connectome map of a fly's actual neurons and connections, and placed it inside an AI-generated world.\n\nA simulated brain exploring a simulated reality.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3my4xspgnf22t",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-18T06:23:59.004Z",
      "likes": 95,
      "replies": 3,
      "reposts": 9,
      "score": 6.5,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2,
        "recency": 0.8,
        "age_hours": 35
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3my47ihhocc2t",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "A consequential choice will be made soon by government and companies as they are increasingly flooded with agentic AI inquiries that overcome the frictions that gated access (see the graphs - it has already started!)\n\nTwo options: do you make services worse or better as a result?",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3my47ihhocc2t",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-17T23:08:45.300Z",
      "likes": 101,
      "replies": 10,
      "reposts": 15,
      "score": 6.5,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 2.1,
        "recency": 0.7,
        "age_hours": 42.2
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:flxq4uyjfotciovpw3x3fxnu/app.bsky.feed.post/3mya65d6mns2y",
      "handle": "emollick.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Ethan Mollick",
      "text": "Writing good STATA code was important for my academic career. It looks like that skill is largely becoming obsolete post Sonnet 4.6. (Also take this is as a notice to academics who still think of AI in terms of chatbots, not agents, that a lot has changed in a year) \n\nPaper: cepr.org/voxeu/column...",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/emollick.bsky.social/post/3mya65d6mns2y",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-19T12:55:16.920Z",
      "likes": 36,
      "replies": 3,
      "reposts": 3,
      "score": 6.2,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.7,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 4.5
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:rrjvo5jwuateqep2i7ih5ckl/app.bsky.feed.post/3my663i2aqc2h",
      "handle": "cfiesler.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Casey Fiesler",
      "text": "I've seen a lot of concerns about \"tracking,\" profiling, and even assumptions that Dexcom is selling data, reporting back to insurance providers, or using AI to manipulate pricing. The tracking language isn't new and seems to mostly apply to website cookies, and the rest is speculation.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/cfiesler.bsky.social/post/3my663i2aqc2h",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-18T17:48:55.437Z",
      "likes": 17,
      "replies": 1,
      "reposts": 1,
      "score": 5.2,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1.3,
        "recency": 0.9,
        "age_hours": 23.6
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3myahd52q3s2h",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "One of the co-founders of Anthropic has declared that the Singularity has begun. (From Jack Clark's personal newsletter)",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3myahd52q3s2h",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-19T15:39:35.505Z",
      "likes": 4,
      "replies": 2,
      "reposts": 1,
      "score": 5,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 1,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 1.7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3myahd6eb722h",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "Other questions must come first: must there be a persistent, always on AI for hard take-off? That's a design choice: why would we do that if we believed in hard take-off? I feel like there are many brakes that can be applied, and many astounding and/or negligent things have to happen to get there.",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3myahd6eb722h",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-19T15:39:35.511Z",
      "likes": 5,
      "replies": 1,
      "reposts": 0,
      "score": 4.8,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 0.9,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 1.7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:3igkkqe5nkm66olc4y2syzpy/app.bsky.feed.post/3myahd6e7ak2h",
      "handle": "markriedl.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Mark Riedl",
      "text": "(Before anyone jumps on me: I don't buy it when people say we don't \"understand\" how AI works now. We do. We might not be able to intuit how an LM produces any given behavior in the moment, but we know how the tech works and can trace every computation if we wanted to.)",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/markriedl.bsky.social/post/3myahd6e7ak2h",
      "posted_at": "2026-10-19T15:39:35.509Z",
      "likes": 5,
      "replies": 1,
      "reposts": 0,
      "score": 4.8,
      "score_parts": {
        "engagement": 0.9,
        "recency": 1,
        "age_hours": 1.7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "at://did:plc:rrjvo5jwuateqep2i7ih5ckl/app.bsky.feed.post/3my6beckgfs2i",
      "handle": "cfiesler.bsky.social",
      "display_name": "Casey Fiesler",
      "text": "My guess is that the ownership thing is to keep users from contributing to training competing AI systems.",
